From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] bl2: print the banner, the DDR result and failures only

At 115 200 baud each console character costs BL2 87 us, and it printed
about 1 400 of them on every boot, step marks for each load, the DDR
package fields piece by piece, the PLL and RTC steps: BL2 ran 150 ms with
them and 100 ms without any (LOG_LEVEL 1, on the stand).

Keep the banner, "DDR BIST PASS" and every failure message; the step marks
become INFO, and INFO is compiled out below LOG_LEVEL_INFO, strings
included. A build with LOG_LEVEL 3 prints them all again.
---
 include/debug.h                 |  8 ++++++++
 lib/cpu/riscv/bl2_helper.c      |  2 +-
 lib/utils/decompress.c          |  2 +-
 plat/cv181x/bl2/bl2_opt.c       | 34 +++++++++++++++++-----------------
 plat/cv181x/bl2/sd_fast.c       |  2 +-
 plat/cv181x/ddr/ddr.c           |  4 ++--
 plat/cv181x/ddr/ddr_pkg_info.c  | 30 +++++++++++++++---------------
 plat/cv181x/ddr/phy_pll_init.c  |  2 +-
 plat/cv181x/platform.c          | 18 +++++++++---------
 plat/cv181x/security/security.c |  4 ++--
 10 files changed, 57 insertions(+), 49 deletions(-)
diff --git a/include/debug.h b/include/debug.h
index b178363..83d8e08 100644
--- a/include/debug.h
+++ b/include/debug.h
@@ -39,7 +39,15 @@ int putchar_l(int c, int level);
 #define ERROR(...) tf_printf(MSG_ERROR " E:" __VA_ARGS__)
 #define WARN(...) tf_printf(MSG_WARN " W:" __VA_ARGS__)
 #define NOTICE(...) tf_printf(MSG_NOTICE __VA_ARGS__)
+/*
+ * Below LOG_LEVEL_INFO, INFO() is compiled out (its strings too); the
+ * arguments stay referenced, so no variable becomes unused.
+ */
+#if LOG_LEVEL >= LOG_LEVEL_INFO
 #define INFO(...) tf_printf(MSG_INFO " I:" __VA_ARGS__)
+#else
+#define INFO(...) do { if (0) tf_printf(MSG_INFO " I:" __VA_ARGS__); } while (0)
+#endif
 
 #if LOG_LEVEL >= LOG_LEVEL_VERBOSE
 #define VERBOSE(...) tf_printf(MSG_VERBOSE __VA_ARGS__)
